  "evidence_scope": "Pinned Marker3 V5 factory selected RTV1. Native RTV1 Init, CreatePenCanvas, actual SPTextureBitmap::GetSubBitmap(0), SetBuffer, three native AddPoint calls, SendDataToGPU, Update(false), and Draw execute. Embedded mask/composite shaders and actual Renderer GL state/draw calls execute in host Mesa GLES; native handles are mapped to host Mesa objects. Synthetic direct point stream is injected at RT AddPoint, rather than produced by saved ObjectStroke replay. Marker3 native RT has zero color state, so this records a zero-color backend contract only, not visible ink or app admission. This capture intentionally supplies the mask bitmap itself as Draw output, causing framebuffer feedback aliasing; it is a native draw-state/negative-control fixture, not a valid paint readback oracle.",
